# (including the flag+size part)
# Actually wait - looking at the tmux capture again:
# " [1m[31m   5.0[39m MiB █████████▉▏bigfile[0m[39m[49m"
# The space (flag) BEFORE the number is NOT colored
# Then [1m][31m] applies to just "   5.0"
# Then [39m] to reset fg color
# Then " MiB █████████▉▏bigfile" is normal text
# Then [0m][39m][49m] at the end resets everything

# Let me look at what [49m is: it's "default background color"
# So the final codes: \033[0m (full reset) + \033[39m (default fg) + \033[49m (default bg)

# For my implementation:
# Non-selected item format:
# flag_char (1) + \033[1;31m + number_str + \033[39m + " " + unit + " " + bar + name_colored + \033[0m\033[39m\033[49m

# But the size field "   5.0 MiB" needs to be split into number "   5.0" and unit " MiB"
# That's complex. Let me see if just applying bold-red to the whole size field works.

